  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#the-input-element:dom-fae-form\n\n> readonly attribute FileList? files;\n\nSeaching [online](http://stackoverflow.com/questions/1017224/dynamically-set-value-of-a-file-input) points to the idea that malicious authors could set `input.files` to include a file on the user's local file system, leaking their data. However, nowadays, if they had access to a `FileList` with a local file, they can already read it through `FileReader` and send it through XHR.\n\nIn fact, `input.files` is already writable on Blink and WebKit, since [this commit](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/blink/+/21bce2e671e41b4e4a7e7e3508dcc03439ae3e9e). [WebKit bug](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=87154). As a result, the issue was studied by [WHATWG](https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=22682) and [Mozilla](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=757664). There seems to be patches being worked on for Firefox by bz and sicking. I believe there is no reason not to move forward with that change, but welcome discussing it further.\n\nThe IDL line in Blink is [the following](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/blink/+/master/Source/core/html/HTMLInputElement.idl#38):\n\n> attribute FileList? files;\n\nHere is a simple test that goes green if it allows setting `input.files`: https://output.jsbin.com/yavebam.\n",
